note bottom
  GOVERNANCE
  - iam.users is an account; profiles.persons is the human identity.
  - Clinical aggregates carry explicit custody for tenant isolation and RLS.
  - Legal bases, consent, authorization and informed consent are separate records.
  - State transitions are governed in Module 32.
  - Frontend pages consume Module 30 projections, never raw ORM entities.
  - Module 52 governs interoperable ingestion, identity resolution, lineage and controlled exports.
  - Module 53 governs interventions, surgery, anesthesia, implants, recovery and outcomes.
  - PostgreSQL remains canonical; Modules 54-63 govern specialized derived stores.
  - Cross-store writes use transactional outbox and persistent idempotent workers, never unsafe dual writes.
  - Deletion, legal hold, retention and reconciliation propagate across every secondary store.
  - Dynamic enumerations resolve through terminology and system context.
  - All writes use named constraints, optimistic concurrency and idempotency where required.
end note

note as INDEX_SCOPE
  INDEX SCOPE
  This module is architectural/use-case/deployment documentation and has no
  owned relational tables. Physical indexes are declared in the owning data modules.
end note

